# SolidWorks MCP (Marengo)

- Open **`marengo.code-workspace`** (marengo + solidworks-mcp) for CAD + MCP worker edits.
- After changing `solidworks-mcp` worker or TS: `npm run build` in `solidworks-mcp`, then **restart the SolidWorks MCP server** in Cursor (MCP panel → restart, or Reload Window). Stale MCP causes wrong URDF/readiness results.
- Verify tools: `npm run validate:tools` in `solidworks-mcp` (requires SolidWorks running).
- `solidworks_status` returns `mcpVersion`; if missing or old after a build, restart MCP.
- CAD allowed root: **`C:/code/marengo`** only (`SOLIDWORKS_MCP_ALLOWED_ROOTS`).
- Root assembly target: `cad/assemblies/marengo.SLDASM`.
- MCP is **audit-first**: conventions, design package, URDF readiness, postcheck, hardware coverage — no URDF writer or `insert_component` yet.
- **Never parallelize SolidWorks MCP tool calls** — COM is STA; concurrent workers crash SolidWorks (see `solidworks-mcp/docs/troubleshooting.md`). Workers are serialized in 0.3.1+, but still run audits one tool at a time.
- **Never** run destructive CAD automation unless the user explicitly asked in that turn. All of these require `--confirm` (scripts) or `confirm: true` (MCP `marengo_torso_frame_build`): `torso-frame-layout-place.mjs`, `torso-frame-autobuild.mjs`, `torso-frame-layout-sync.mjs`, `torso-frame-layout-sync-continue.mjs`, `torso-frame-remate.mjs`. Do not “fix” assemblies by deleting mates or snapping transforms without permission.
- Before CAD or automation edits: follow [worktree-safety.mdc](./worktree-safety.mdc) — commit or stash/backup dirty work first; never restore/checkout binary CAD over uncommitted changes.
- URDF export is **manual** (Brawner) → `assets/urdf/marengo.urdf`; joint truth in `hardware/docs/kinematics.md`.
- Standards: [cad/README.md](../../cad/README.md).
